# PDF Engine

## Mục tiêu

PDF Engine là hệ thống xử lý tài liệu PDF cho việc tạo, chỉnh sửa, trích xuất nội dung, và chuyển đổi. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, PDF Engine được sử dụng cho các ứng dụng như invoice generation, report creation, document merging, OCR processing, và data extraction. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc implement PDF processing systems hiệu quả và reliable.

PDF processing đòi hỏi sự hiểu biết về PDF format, rendering engines, security considerations, và performance optimization. Một PDF engine tốt cần handle được các loại documents khác nhau từ simple text documents đến complex forms với embedded images và fonts.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Library Selection**

Choose appropriate PDF library. Consider performance needs. Evaluate rendering quality. Check browser compatibility. Consider commercial vs open source.

**2. Document Generation**

Use templates for consistency. Handle complex layouts. Support dynamic content. Include proper fonts. Optimize for file size.

**3. Text Extraction**

Extract text accurately. Handle multiple encodings. Preserve structure. Support OCR when needed. Handle images with text.

**4. Security Considerations**

Sanitize PDF inputs. Prevent malicious PDFs. Handle password-protected files. Validate content. Monitor for exploits.

**5. Performance Optimization**

Use streaming for large files. Cache rendered pages. Optimize memory usage. Use worker threads. Process in batches.

**6. Template Management**

Store templates securely. Version control templates. Validate template syntax. Support template inheritance. Monitor template usage.

**7. Data Binding**

Bind data to templates. Handle nested data. Support conditions. Include formatting. Validate data types.

**8. Conversion Formats**

Support multiple output formats. PDF/A for archival. PDF/UA for accessibility. Optimize for web. Handle conversion errors.

**9. Accessibility**

Support screen readers. Include alt text. Create tagged PDFs. Follow PDF/UA standards. Test accessibility.

**10. Compliance**

Follow PDF standards. Support PDF/A, PDF/X. Include metadata. Support digital signatures. Maintain audit trails.

## Checklist

- [ ] PDF library selected
- [ ] Document generation implemented
- [ ] Text extraction set up
- [ ] OCR integration configured
- [ ] Template system designed
- [ ] Security measures implemented
- [ ] Performance optimized
- [ ] Accessibility supported
- [ ] Conversion formats defined
- [ ] Monitoring set up

## Anti Pattern

**1. Loading Entire PDFs into Memory**

Loading large PDFs fully into memory. Memory exhaustion. Performance degradation. Use streaming instead.

**2. Ignoring Font Embedding**

Not embedding fonts. Cross-platform issues. Missing characters. Embed all fonts.

**3. No Input Validation**

Processing untrusted PDFs. Security vulnerabilities. Malicious content. Always validate.

**4. Synchronous Processing**

Processing PDFs on main thread. UI blocking. Poor responsiveness. Use async/workers.

**5. Hardcoded Templates**

Embedding templates in code. No reusability. Difficult updates. Use template management system.

## Best Practice

**1. PDF Generation với Puppeteer**

```typescript
// services/pdf-generator.service.ts
import puppeteer, { Browser, PDFOptions } from 'puppeteer';
import { compile } from 'handlebars';
import fs from 'fs/promises';
import path from 'path';

interface PDFTemplate {
  name: string;
  html: string;
  styles?: string;
}

interface PDFData {
  [key: string]: any;
}

class PDFGeneratorService {
  private browser: Browser | null = null;
  private templates: Map<string, HandlebarsTemplateDelegate> = new Map();

  async initialize(): Promise<void> {
    this.browser = await puppeteer.launch({
      headless: true,
      args: [
        '--no-sandbox',
        '--disable-setuid-sandbox',
        '--disable-dev-shm-usage'
      ]
    });
  }

  async registerTemplate(name: string, html: string, styles?: string): Promise<void> {
    const fullHtml = `
      <!DOCTYPE html>
      <html>
        <head>
          <meta charset="utf-8">
          <style>
            ${styles || ''}
            body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 40px; }
            .header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px; }
            .content { line-height: 1.6; }
            .footer { position: fixed; bottom: 0; width: 100%; }
          </style>
        </head>
        <body>
          ${html}
        </body>
      </html>
    `;

    const template = compile(fullHtml);
    this.templates.set(name, template);
  }

  async registerTemplateFromFile(
    name: string,
    templatePath: string,
    stylesPath?: string
  ): Promise<void> {
    const html = await fs.readFile(templatePath, 'utf-8');
    const styles = stylesPath ? await fs.readFile(stylesPath, 'utf-8') : undefined;
    await this.registerTemplate(name, html, styles);
  }

  async generatePDF(
    templateName: string,
    data: PDFData,
    options: PDFOptions = {}
  ): Promise<Buffer> {
    if (!this.browser) {
      await this.initialize();
    }

    const template = this.templates.get(templateName);
    if (!template) {
      throw new Error(`Template not found: ${templateName}`);
    }

    // Compile template with data
    const html = template(data);

    // Create a new page
    const page = await this.browser.newPage();

    try {
      // Set content
      await page.setContent(html, {
        waitUntil: 'networkidle0'
      });

      // Generate PDF
      const pdfOptions: PDFOptions = {
        format: 'A4',
        printBackground: true,
        margin: {
          top: '20mm',
          bottom: '20mm',
          left: '15mm',
          right: '15mm'
        },
        ...options
      };

      const pdfBuffer = await page.pdf(pdfOptions);

      return Buffer.from(pdfBuffer);
    } finally {
      await page.close();
    }
  }

  async generatePDFStream(
    templateName: string,
    data: PDFData,
    options: PDFOptions = {}
  ): Promise<NodeJS.ReadableStream> {
    const buffer = await this.generatePDF(templateName, data, options);
    return Readable.from(buffer);
  }

  async generateBulkPDFs(
    documents: Array<{ templateName: string; data: PDFData; filename: string }>,
    options: PDFOptions = {}
  ): Promise<Map<string, Buffer>> {
    const results = new Map<string, Buffer>();

    // Process in parallel with concurrency limit
    const concurrency = 3;
    const chunks = this.chunkArray(documents, concurrency);

    for (const chunk of chunks) {
      const promises = chunk.map(async (doc) => {
        const buffer = await this.generatePDF(doc.templateName, doc.data, options);
        return { filename: doc.filename, buffer };
      });

      const chunkResults = await Promise.all(promises);
      chunkResults.forEach(({ filename, buffer }) => {
        results.set(filename, buffer);
      });
    }

    return results;
  }

  private chunkArray<T>(array: T[], size: number): T[][] {
    const chunks: T[][] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i += size) {
      chunks.push(array.slice(i, i + size));
    }
    return chunks;
  }

  async shutdown(): Promise<void> {
    if (this.browser) {
      await this.browser.close();
      this.browser = null;
    }
  }
}
```

**2. Text Extraction với pdf-parse**

```typescript
// services/pdf-extractor.service.ts
import fs from 'fs/promises';
import path from 'path';
import pdf from 'pdf-parse';

interface ExtractionResult {
  text: string;
  pages: PageContent[];
  metadata: PDFMetadata;
  outlines: Outline[];
}

interface PageContent {
  pageNumber: number;
  text: string;
  images: ImageInfo[];
  tables: TableInfo[];
}

interface ImageInfo {
  pageNumber: number;
  index: number;
  x: number;
  y: number;
  width: number;
  height: number;
  base64?: string;
}

interface TableInfo {
  pageNumber: number;
  rows: string[][];
  boundingBox: BoundingBox;
}

interface BoundingBox {
  x: number;
  y: number;
  width: number;
  height: number;
}

interface PDFMetadata {
  title?: string;
  author?: string;
  subject?: string;
  keywords?: string;
  creator?: string;
  producer?: string;
  creationDate?: Date;
  modificationDate?: Date;
}

interface Outline {
  title: string;
  level: number;
  pageNumber: number;
  children?: Outline[];
}

class PDFExtractorService {
  async extractText(filePath: string): Promise<string> {
    const dataBuffer = await fs.readFile(filePath);
    const data = await pdf(dataBuffer);
    return data.text;
  }

  async extractFullContent(filePath: string): Promise<ExtractionResult> {
    const dataBuffer = await fs.readFile(filePath);
    const data = await pdf(dataBuffer);

    const pages = await this.extractPageContents(dataBuffer, data);
    const metadata = this.extractMetadata(data);
    const outlines = this.extractOutlines(data);

    return {
      text: data.text,
      pages,
      metadata,
      outlines
    };
  }

  private async extractPageContents(
    dataBuffer: Buffer,
    data: any
  ): Promise<PageContent[]> {
    const pages: PageContent[] = [];

    for (let i = 0; i < data.numpages; i++) {
      // Extract text for each page
      const pageText = data.pages[i]?.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim() || '';

      pages.push({
        pageNumber: i + 1,
        text: pageText,
        images: [], // Images require additional processing
        tables: [] // Tables require specialized extraction
      });
    }

    return pages;
  }

  private extractMetadata(data: any): PDFMetadata {
    return {
      title: data.info?.Title,
      author: data.info?.Author,
      subject: data.info?.Subject,
      keywords: data.info?.Keywords,
      creator: data.info?.Creator,
      producer: data.info?.Producer,
      creationDate: data.info?.CreationDate,
      modificationDate: data.info?.ModDate
    };
  }

  private extractOutlines(data: any): Outline[] {
    // Extract TOC/outlines if available
    // This requires parsing the PDF structure
    return [];
  }

  async extractTextByPage(filePath: string): Promise<string[]> {
    const dataBuffer = await fs.readFile(filePath);
    const data = await pdf(dataBuffer);
    return data.pages.map((page: string) => page.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim());
  }

  async extractTextByArea(
    filePath: string,
    pageNumber: number,
    boundingBox: BoundingBox
  ): Promise<string> {
    const fullText = await this.extractText(filePath);
    const pages = await this.extractTextByPage(filePath);
    // Note: Full bbox extraction requires OCR or advanced parsing
    return pages[pageNumber - 1] || '';
  }
}
